    {
      "@id": "https://marlonbarrios.github.io/hybrid-intelligences/ontology#essay_4",
      "@type": [
        "skos:Concept",
        "hi:NetworkNode"
      ],
      "skos:prefLabel": "Essay 4",
      "skos:definition": "Designing Unstable Landscapes: Improvisational Dance within Cognitive Systems — Essay 4 by Marlon Barrios Solano. First published in Johannes H. Birringer and Josephine Fenger (eds.), Tanz Im Kopf: Dance and Cognition (Broschiert), 2005; dedicated to Francisco Varela. Theorizes hybrid improvisational dance with real-time interactive multimedia as designed cognitive systems through the Unstablelandscape series (1999–2005): post-humanist coupling of bodies, algorithms, and environments; Gibsonian perception-action, embodied cognition, Hayles's posthuman, hyper-plastic embodiment, and distributed cognition across performers and Max/Jitter systems. Republished in the Hybrid Intelligences Hub.",
      "skos:broader": {
        "@id": "https://marlonbarrios.github.io/hybrid-intelligences/ontology#category/practice"
      },
      "skos:inScheme": {
